.TH "DNF5.CONF-VENDORPOLICY-V1_1" "5" "Sep 06, 2026" "" "dnf5"
.SH "نام (NAME)"
dnf5.conf-vendorpolicy-v1_1 \- DNF5 Vendor Change Policy File Reference \- v1.1
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
.sp
This document describes the structure and syntax of the DNF5 Vendor Change Policy
configuration files using \fBversion 1.1\fP and \fBversion 1.2\fP format.
.sp
Version 1.2 is identical to version 1.1 except that it adds support for additional
negated string comparators (see v1.2 comparators).
.sp
For general information about vendor change policy files, see DNF5 Vendor Change Policy File Reference \%<#\:dnf5-vendor-change-policy-label>\&.
.SH FILE STRUCTURE
.SS Required Fields
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \fBversion\fP
String
.sp
Configuration file format version.
.sp
Must be set to \fB\(dq1.1\(dq\fP or \fB\(dq1.2\(dq\fP\&.
.sp
This field is mandatory and must be specified at the top level of the TOML file.
.sp
Example:
.INDENT 7.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
version = \(aq1.2\(aq
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBNote:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
For the configuration file to have any effect on vendor change policy, it must contain
at least one of the supported lists (see below): \fBoutgoing_vendors\fP, \fBincoming_vendors\fP,
\fBequivalent_vendors\fP, \fBoutgoing_packages\fP, or \fBincoming_packages\fP\&.
.sp
If the file contains no lists, it will be loaded and its version will be validated,
but it will not define any rules and will not affect vendor manager behavior.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS Vendor Mapping Definition
.sp
The following vendor lists can be used to define vendor mappings.
All lists are optional and can be freely combined. All conditions are evaluated together.
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \fB[[outgoing_vendors]]\fP
Array of tables
.sp
List of vendors from which changes are allowed (outgoing package vendors).
.TP
.B \fB[[incoming_vendors]]\fP
Array of tables
.sp
List of vendors to which changes are allowed (incoming package vendors).
.TP
.B \fB[[equivalent_vendors]]\fP
Array of tables
.sp
List of vendors that are mutually equivalent. Changes are allowed in both directions
between all vendors in this list.
.sp
\fBNote:\fP
.INDENT 7.0
.INDENT 3.5
\fBequivalent_vendors\fP is actually a shorthand notation. It is equivalent to
listing the same vendors in both \fBoutgoing_vendors\fP and \fBincoming_vendors\fP\&.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBImportant:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
A vendor change during package replacement is allowed \fBonly if both conditions
are met simultaneously\fP:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
The vendor of the outgoing (installed) package is listed in \fBoutgoing_vendors\fP
or \fBequivalent_vendors\fP (or both \fBoutgoing_vendors\fP and \fBequivalent_vendors\fP
are missing, which allows any vendor)
.IP \(bu 2
The vendor of the incoming (new) package is listed in \fBincoming_vendors\fP
or \fBequivalent_vendors\fP (or both \fBincoming_vendors\fP and \fBequivalent_vendors\fP
are missing, which allows any vendor)
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS Vendor Entry Fields
.sp
Each entry in \fB[[outgoing_vendors]]\fP, \fB[[incoming_vendors]]\fP, or \fB[[equivalent_vendors]]\fP
can contain the following fields:
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \fBvendor\fP
String
.sp
Required field.
.sp
Vendor name or pattern for matching.
.TP
.B \fBcomparator\fP
String
.sp
Optional field.
.sp
The matching method to use when comparing vendor strings.
.sp
Default: \fB\(dqEXACT\(dq\fP
.sp
Supported values:
.INDENT 7.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\(dqEXACT\(dq\fP \- exact match (case\-sensitive)
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\(dqIEXACT\(dq\fP \- exact match (case\-insensitive)
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\(dqGLOB\(dq\fP \- glob pattern (case\-sensitive)
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\(dqIGLOB\(dq\fP \- glob pattern (case\-insensitive)
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\(dqREGEX\(dq\fP \- regular expression (case\-sensitive)
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\(dqIREGEX\(dq\fP \- regular expression (case\-insensitive)
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\(dqCONTAINS\(dq\fP \- contains string (case\-sensitive)
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\(dqICONTAINS\(dq\fP \- contains string (case\-insensitive)
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\(dqSTARTSWITH\(dq\fP \- starts with (case\-sensitive)
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\(dqISTARTSWITH\(dq\fP \- starts with (case\-insensitive)
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\(dqENDSWITH\(dq\fP \- ends with (case\-sensitive)
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\(dqIENDSWITH\(dq\fP \- ends with (case\-insensitive)
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\(dqNOT_EXACT\(dq\fP, \fB\(dqNOT_IEXACT\(dq\fP, \fB\(dqNOT_GLOB\(dq\fP, \fB\(dqNOT_IGLOB\(dq\fP, \fB\(dqNOT_CONTAINS\(dq\fP, \fB\(dqNOT_ICONTAINS\(dq\fP \- negated variants
.UNINDENT
.sp
Additional negated comparators available in \fBversion 1.2\fP:
.INDENT 7.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\(dqNOT_STARTSWITH\(dq\fP \- does not start with (case\-sensitive)
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\(dqNOT_ISTARTSWITH\(dq\fP \- does not start with (case\-insensitive)
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\(dqNOT_ENDSWITH\(dq\fP \- does not end with (case\-sensitive)
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\(dqNOT_IENDSWITH\(dq\fP \- does not end with (case\-insensitive)
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\(dqNOT_REGEX\(dq\fP \- does not match regular expression (case\-sensitive)
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\(dqNOT_IREGEX\(dq\fP \- does not match regular expression (case\-insensitive)
.UNINDENT
.TP
.B \fBexclude\fP
Boolean
.sp
Optional field.
.sp
If \fBtrue\fP, the vendor is excluded from the rule. This is useful for defining
exceptions to more general rules. Rules (vendor entries) are processed in the order
they are defined. This means that an exclude rule must appear before the rules
from which the vendor should be excluded.
.sp
Default: \fBfalse\fP
.UNINDENT
.SS Package Filtering
.sp
Vendor change policies can be further restricted to apply only to specific packages
using package filters. These are optional and allow fine\-grained control over which
packages are allowed to change vendors.
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \fB[[outgoing_packages]]\fP
Array of tables
.sp
List of package filters that restrict which outgoing (installed) packages are
allowed to change vendors. If omitted, all packages are allowed to change from
their current vendor.
.TP
.B \fB[[incoming_packages]]\fP
Array of tables
.sp
List of package filters that restrict which incoming (new) packages are allowed
to be installed with a vendor change. If omitted, all packages are allowed to
be installed regardless of vendor.
.UNINDENT
.SS Package Filter Entry Fields
.sp
Each entry in \fB[[outgoing_packages]]\fP or \fB[[incoming_packages]]\fP can contain:
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \fBfilters\fP
Array of tables
.sp
Required field.
.sp
List of filter conditions that must all match for the package to be affected by
this rule. Each filter is a table with the following fields:
.INDENT 7.0
.TP
.B \fBfilter\fP
String
.sp
Required field.
.sp
The package attribute to filter on.
.sp
Supported values:
.INDENT 7.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\(dqname\(dq\fP \- package name
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\(dqsource_name\(dq\fP \- source package name
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\(dqevr\(dq\fP \- Epoch\-Version\-Release string
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\(dqepoch\(dq\fP \- epoch number
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\(dqversion\(dq\fP \- version string
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\(dqrelease\(dq\fP \- release string
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\(dqarch\(dq\fP \- package architecture
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\(dqrepoid\(dq\fP \- repository ID
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\(dqcmdline_repo\(dq\fP \- whether the package is from command\-line repository (boolean)
.UNINDENT
.TP
.B \fBvalue\fP
String
.sp
Required field.
.sp
The value to match against.
.INDENT 7.0
.IP \(bu 2
For \fBcmdline_repo\fP filter, use \fB\(dqtrue\(dq\fP/\fB\(dq1\(dq\fP or \fB\(dqfalse\(dq\fP/\fB\(dq0\(dq\fP
.IP \(bu 2
For \fBepoch\fP filter, use a numeric string (e.g., \fB\(dq0\(dq\fP, \fB\(dq1\(dq\fP)
.IP \(bu 2
For other filters, use appropriate string values
.UNINDENT
.TP
.B \fBcomparator\fP
String
.sp
Optional field.
.sp
The matching method to use.
.sp
Default: \fB\(dqEXACT\(dq\fP
.sp
\fBFor string\-based filters\fP (\fBname\fP, \fBsource_name\fP, \fBarch\fP, \fBrepoid\fP):
.sp
Same values as for vendor comparator: \fBEXACT\fP, \fBNOT_EXACT\fP, \fBIEXACT\fP,
\fBNOT_IEXACT\fP, \fBCONTAINS\fP, \fBNOT_CONTAINS\fP, \fBICONTAINS\fP, \fBNOT_ICONTAINS\fP,
\fBSTARTSWITH\fP, \fBISTARTSWITH\fP, \fBENDSWITH\fP, \fBIENDSWITH\fP, \fBREGEX\fP,
\fBIREGEX\fP, \fBGLOB\fP, \fBNOT_GLOB\fP, \fBIGLOB\fP, \fBNOT_IGLOB\fP
.sp
Version 1.2 additionally supports: \fBNOT_STARTSWITH\fP, \fBNOT_ISTARTSWITH\fP,
\fBNOT_ENDSWITH\fP, \fBNOT_IENDSWITH\fP, \fBNOT_REGEX\fP, \fBNOT_IREGEX\fP
.sp
\fBFor version\-based filters\fP (\fBevr\fP, \fBepoch\fP, \fBversion\fP, \fBrelease\fP):
.INDENT 7.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\(dqEXACT\(dq\fP \- equal to
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\(dqNOT_EXACT\(dq\fP \- not equal to
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\(dqGT\(dq\fP \- greater than
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\(dqGTE\(dq\fP \- greater than or equal to
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\(dqLT\(dq\fP \- less than
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\(dqLTE\(dq\fP \- less than or equal to
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBNote:\fP
.INDENT 7.0
.INDENT 3.5
Version\-based filters use proper RPM version comparison semantics
instead of lexical string comparison. This ensures correct version
ordering (e.g., \(dq1.10\(dq > \(dq1.9\(dq).
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBNote:\fP
.INDENT 7.0
.INDENT 3.5
The \fBcmdline_repo\fP filter only supports \fB\(dqEXACT\(dq\fP comparator.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.TP
.B \fBexclude\fP
Boolean
.sp
Optional field.
.sp
If \fBtrue\fP, packages matching the filters are excluded from the rule. This is
useful for defining exceptions. Exclusion rules must appear before the rules
from which packages should be excluded.
.sp
Default: \fBfalse\fP
.UNINDENT
.SH "مثال‌ها (EXAMPLES)"
.SS Example 1: Allow change from \(dqVendorA\(dq to \(dqVendorB\(dq
.sp
This example shows the minimal required configuration, allowing a change from
\(dqVendorA\(dq to \(dqVendorB\(dq, but not the reverse.
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
version = \(aq1.2\(aq

[[outgoing_vendors]]
vendor = \(aqVendorA\(aq

[[incoming_vendors]]
vendor = \(aqVendorB\(aq
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS Example 2: Allow change from any vendor to \(dqMy Trusted Vendor\(dq
.sp
This example shows allowing a change from any vendor to \(dqMy Trusted Vendor\(dq,
but not the reverse. Missing \fBoutgoing_vendors\fP means any vendor is allowed.
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
version = \(aq1.2\(aq

[[incoming_vendors]]
vendor = \(aqMy Trusted Vendor\(aq
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS Example 3: Equivalent vendors
.sp
This example shows vendors that are mutually equivalent, allowing changes
in both directions.
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
version = \(aq1.2\(aq

# All following vendors are mutually equivalent
[[equivalent_vendors]]
vendor = \(aqFedora Project\(aq

[[equivalent_vendors]]
vendor = \(aqRed Hat\(aq
comparator = \(aqISTARTSWITH\(aq

[[equivalent_vendors]]
vendor = \(aqCentOS\(aq
comparator = \(aqISTARTSWITH\(aq
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS Example 4: Equivalent vendors with an exclusion
.sp
This example shows a vendor policy for SUSE\-related vendors with an exclusion
for openSUSE Build Service.
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
version = \(aq1.2\(aq

# All following vendors are mutually equivalent except excluded ones
[[equivalent_vendors]]
vendor = \(aqopenSUSE Build Service\(aq
comparator = \(aqISTARTSWITH\(aq
exclude = true

[[equivalent_vendors]]
vendor = \(aqSUSE\(aq
comparator = \(aqISTARTSWITH\(aq

[[equivalent_vendors]]
vendor = \(aqopenSUSE\(aq
comparator = \(aqISTARTSWITH\(aq
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS Example 5: Combining equivalent vendors with incoming vendors
.sp
This example demonstrates combining \fBequivalent_vendors\fP with \fBincoming_vendors\fP,
a feature introduced in version \fB\(dq1.1\(dq\fP\&. \(dqFirst Vendor\(dq and \(dqSecond Vendor\(dq are mutually
equivalent, and both can change to \(dqThird Vendor\(dq.
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
version = \(aq1.2\(aq

[[equivalent_vendors]]
vendor = \(aqFirst Vendor\(aq

[[equivalent_vendors]]
vendor = \(aqSecond Vendor\(aq

[[incoming_vendors]]
vendor = \(aqThird Vendor\(aq
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS Example 6: Allow command\-line packages from any vendor
.sp
This example allows installing packages from the command\-line repository
from any vendor, bypassing vendor restrictions.
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
version = \(aq1.2\(aq

[[incoming_packages]]
filters = [
  { filter = \(aqcmdline_repo\(aq, value = \(aqtrue\(aq }
]
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS Example 7: Command\-line packages with exclusion
.sp
This example allows installing packages from the command\-line repository
from any vendor, except for packages whose names start with \(dqmypackage\(dq.
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
version = \(aq1.2\(aq

[[incoming_packages]]
filters = [
  { filter = \(aqname\(aq, value = \(aqmypackage\(aq, comparator = \(aqSTARTSWITH\(aq }
]
exclude = true

[[incoming_packages]]
filters = [
  { filter = \(aqcmdline_repo\(aq, value = \(aqtrue\(aq }
]
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS Example 8: Allow change from any vendor to specific one with package filtering
.sp
This example allows a change from any vendor to \(dqMy Vendor\(dq, but
only for incoming packages whose source package name is \(dqmypackage\(dq and
version is greater than or equal to \(dq2.0\(dq.
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
version = \(aq1.2\(aq

[[incoming_packages]]
filters = [
  { filter = \(aqsource_name\(aq, value = \(aqmypackage\(aq },
  { filter = \(aqversion\(aq, value = \(aq2.0\(aq, comparator = \(aqGTE\(aq }
]

[[incoming_vendors]]
vendor = \(aqMy Vendor\(aq
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SH "همچنین ببینید (SEE ALSO)"
.INDENT 0.0
